WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
A mayor steps up to the microphone
and says just three words:

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.030
«Je suis inquiet.» That evening,

3
00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.900
a reporter writes it up:

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.360
«Le maire a dit qu'il…»
and stops at the verb.

5
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.930
The mayor's words are about to change.

6
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.860
Not because anyone misheard him,

7
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.310
and nobody will call it a mistake.

8
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.520
So what happens to a verb when it passes

9
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.210
from someone's mouth into a report?

10
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.830
Why does it slide back in time?

11
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.920
In this mission, you'll walk
down the backshift staircase,

12
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.510
pairing each quote with its report.

13
00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.010
Then you'll report Karim's promise,

14
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.100
«Je partirai demain», on
a timeline of your own.

15
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.260
Your mission: work out the rule,

16
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.640
and report any quote like a journalist.
